INT. CANDLELIT SALON - NIGHT - 1789

Red velvet, gilt mirrors, a card table scattered with coins. A door ajar to a dark corridor. Outside, a mob's murmur rises like surf.

CAPTAIN LUCIEN (30s, powdered wig, frayed uniform) holds a rapier. Across the table stands SERGEANT ROQUE (40s, scarred cheek, soldier's pistol). Between them, trembling under a lace shawl, MADAME OUDIN (60s, rouged, jeweled fingers) clings to the back of a chair.

They freeze. All three. Candle flames waver.

LUCIEN
Roque. Lower it.

ROQUE
Not till he drops the blade.

LUCIEN
He won't.

ROQUE
Then neither will I.

Madame Oudin lets out a thin whimper. The mob outside surges. A bottle shatters against the shutters.

LUCIEN
Madame, behind me.

She scrambles to him. Roque tracks her with the pistol. Lucien shifts the rapier a hair, covering her. Roque advances one step. Lucien retreats, shoving the table. Coins ring on the floor.

They lunge together. Steel meets steel and clashes against the pistol barrel. A shot cracks. The mirror shatters. All three flinch.

Silence. Smoke drifts. No one has fallen.

MADAME OUDIN
(a whisper)
Oh, my.

In the corridor, boots pound closer.
